${H1}Removing${RST}

${CMD}rm${RST} removes a file at once and for good. There is no Trash and no undo.

  ${CMD}ls${RST}                 ${DIM}# look first${RST}
  ${CMD}rm backup.txt${RST}      ${DIM}# remove it${RST}
  ${CMD}ls${RST}                 ${DIM}# it is gone${RST}

List before you remove: you, or an assistant typing for you.

${INSTR}${G_PLAY} Try all three, then type ${CMD}next${INSTR}.${RST}
EOF
